<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15121" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄριστον</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>morning meal, breakfast,</i>
			twice in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐντύνοντ᾽ ἄ. ἅμ᾽ ἠοῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					16.2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.124
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄριστα, δεῖπνα, δόρπα θ᾽ αἱρεῖσθαι
					τρίτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					182
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ag.</u>
				331
			</span></i>: later, <i>breakfast</i> was called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκράτισμα,</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄριστον</span> was the midday meal, our <i>luncheon,</i> cf.
				<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.90
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.81
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. αἱρεῖσθαι, ποιεῖσθαι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.78
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπ᾽ ἀρίστου μέχρι δείλης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					619a15
				</span></i>
			. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ</span>; 
				contr.
			 from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ</span>(<i>y</i>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ερι-στον,</span>
			cf. Goth. <i>air,</i> OHG. <i>ēr</i> 'early', Avest.
				<i>ayar[schwa]</i> 'day'; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ</span>(<i>y</i>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ερ</span>- in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦρι, ἠέριος;
			-στο-</span> from <i>-d-to-,</i> root <i>ed-</i>
		'eat'.]</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
